{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession","id":113788,"title":"Ghosts and Possession?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-15T20:50:08-07:00","id":113788,"title":"Ghosts and Possession?","content":"Okay, so with the GMC update, it states that ghosts can only possess something that has the Open condition which requires that something to be one of the ghost's anchors, correct? Since most anchors tend to be locations or objects, I assume most ghosts don't seem capable of possessing humans or supernatural beings, unless they're anchored to a specific individual? If that's the case, then I can't, for example, use the Skinrider from the nWoD Core book and hijack a random person's body that happened to be walking by the Skinrider's anchor? The Skinrider could only possess things that are part of his anchors, which generally tend to be objects. Darn, I really liked the idea of a ghost jumping around from human host to human host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T21:52:41-07:00","id":113834,"title":"","content":"Consider the following for a moment:<br /> <br /> a) Mechanically speaking a Skinrider is, in GMC's mechanics, near the upper bound of power for non-Underworld ghosts and its ability to possess people is reflective of this - Dave Brookshaw has noted that ghosts strong enough to possess people are rare.<br /> b) Influences as Conditions for Manifestation are allowed to go a little abstract - dog-spirits can presumably still treat people who have sufficient doglike traits as Resonant, and Anchors aren't much different.<br /> c) Anchors, like a spirit's Influences, are non-specific in scope - a ghost whose identity is bound up in the value of the locket given to them by their beloved does not have power over that locket as a function of &quot;That Locket&quot; being an Anchor, but as a function of the locket falling under the auspices of that ghost's Anchor Influence, which is broader than &quot;their beloved locket&quot; even if that's all they ever use the Influence for. Could be that they have an Influence over Lockets, but more likely they've anchored their identity in the emotional context that gave the locket value.<br /> d) It is in keeping with the literature that prolonged use of or exposure to haunted items or places opens one up to ghostly influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T01:23:31-07:00","id":113914,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Also, bear in mind that once a Ghost gets powerful enough to use its Influence creatively, it can <i>make</i> &quot;Open&quot; on targets that come into contact with its Anchor.<br /> <br /> A skinrider would be a Rank 3-5 ghost which kept its Influence: Anchor without diversifying. It's therefore good at manipulating its manifestation conditions, and can possess people who have too much contact with its anchors.<br /> <br /> A Kerberos would be a high Rank ghost which ditched Anchor for Influence over its Dominion. Very powerful in the Underworld, can't leave.<br /> <br /> A Geist would be a mid-high Rank ghost which went for Influence over a thematic form of death, and picked up the Manifestation that lets it make a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> That Manifestation isn't written up, and might not be even if Geist ever gets a GMC update, but that's the design intention. Think of it as a cross, mechanically, between Claim and the Strix &quot;Synthesis&quot; power, which is the one the owls use to &quot;embrace&quot; new vampires. Sin-Eaters aren't &quot;ghost Claimed&quot; - they're a major template, not a minor one - but that's the general notion. GMC's ephemeral entities rules were a complex four-way dance of allowing mortal hunters to act like the Winchester brothers, laying groundwork for Demon and Idigam Chronicle, and leaving the door ajar in case the stars align and we can do a deeper look at ghosts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:44:24-07:00","id":113935,"title":"","content":"So Are Keberoi definitively ghosts in GMC?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T05:47:00-07:00","id":113988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession#post113788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Skinrider could only possess things that are part of his anchors, which generally tend to be objects. Darn, I really liked the idea of a ghost jumping around from human host to human host.</div> </div> </div> </div> Influence (Anchor) 4. Create Anchor. Use on person. Jump into said person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T05:51:33-07:00","id":113989,"title":"","content":"I would love to have a book taking a deeper look at ghosts. There's a lot available out there; but the Underworld is vast, and ghosts are like pawns in chess: they all get used, abused, and exploited by the major splats but every now and then they get across the board and become a Queen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:57:47-07:00","id":114026,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses, everyone! I was under the impression that Skinriders were Rank 2 ghosts because they haven't crossed over to the Underworld yet for some reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:07:34-07:00","id":114036,"title":"","content":"How can a Ghost of rank 3+ have Influence: Anchor? You can only get influence 3+ if you are in the underworld, and you only go to the underworld if you lose all your anchors, or am I missing something?<br /> <br /> Also, I never understand where do old ghosts get their essence from, as nobody remembers most of them. Are all old ghosts ghosts from famous people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/524-angrycucaracha","name":"AngryCucaracha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:57:24-07:00","id":114060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AngryCucaracha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=114036#post114036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Ghost of rank 3+ have Influence: Anchor? You can only get influence 3+ if you are in the underworld, and you only go to the underworld if you lose all your anchors, or am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anchor is a category of Influence, not an Influence itself. Isaac Donahue's ghost has only two dots of Influence: Sadness and hasn't turned into anything more unusual than a ghost - he's bound up his identity in the depression that led him to take his own life, and if he raised his Rank in the Underworld he could raise that Influence to three dots.<br /> <br /> GMC's rules for &quot;losing all your anchors&quot; are &quot;run out of Essence due to the bleed suffered from remaining outside the radius of an Anchor Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I never understand where do old ghosts get their essence from, as nobody remembers most of them. Are all old ghosts ghosts from famous people? </div> </div> </div>Avernian Gates and the ability to communicate one's identity to people go a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:51:38-07:00","id":114147,"title":"","content":"How do Sin-Eaters summon ghosts from the Underworld? Can they use the Bind Anchor ceremony on ghosts in the Underworld to give them an anchor and allow them to return? If so, how does the ghost appear? Is it just poof and the ghost appears once it's been given a new anchor, or does something else happen first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T15:13:43-07:00","id":114354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=114147#post114147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Sin-Eaters summon ghosts from the Underworld? Can they use the Bind Anchor ceremony on ghosts in the Underworld to give them an anchor and allow them to return? If so, how does the ghost appear? Is it just poof and the ghost appears once it's been given a new anchor, or does something else happen first?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it creates the Anchor condition on an item/area after creating an Avernian Gateway Condition to the Ghost in the Underworld. It's basically the inverse of what happens when they run out of Essence due to bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:09:08-07:00","id":114715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=114026#post114026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the responses, everyone! I was under the impression that Skinriders were Rank 2 ghosts because they haven't crossed over to the Underworld yet for some reason</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, there's always going to be some changes and things between editions. Things aren't a perfect match. And, who's to say a Skinrider hadn't been to the Underworld... and came back? There's lots of possibilities, and I'm loathe to say one or another. There are always exceptions to the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T04:22:58-07:00","id":118382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=113914#post113914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That Manifestation isn't written up, and might not be even if Geist ever gets a GMC update, but that's the design intention. Think of it as a cross, mechanically, between Claim and the Strix &quot;Synthesis&quot; power, which is the one the owls use to &quot;embrace&quot; new vampires. Sin-Eaters aren't &quot;ghost Claimed&quot; - they're a major template, not a minor one - but that's the general notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>What ever the idea behind Geist's methaphysics, I relly hope there will be some factor that explains how Sin Eaters are able to be so utterly terrifyingly powerful. The Divine Fire of the Prometheans is probably the most mythical and powerful feeling of the different sources of powers the major templates in NWoD use, with the Mummy's rite of return and the Mages' access to the source code of the universe as close seconds. With the raw amount of fuck you a Sin Eater can put out compared to most other splats they feel like their abilities should be based on something that's at least as epic in scope.<br /> Being the product of a (comparatively) mundane manifestation used by a Ghost/spirit hybrid just never really fit how absolutely scary a Sin-Eater is when they let loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}